# Docker build context filter.
#
# The build context is the whole repo. Without this, every build copies ~470 MB of
# virtualenvs, node_modules and live runtime state, and risks baking secrets into
# image layers. Keep this list in sync with .gitignore for anything secret.

# --- VCS / tooling caches ----------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.import_linter_cache/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.vite/
**/build/
**/*.egg-info/

# --- Runtime state: must never enter an image --------------------------------
# The backend rewrites config.yaml and owns data/ at runtime; both arrive as
# volumes. A stale copy baked into the image would mask the volume on first run.
claudio-backend/data/
claudio-frontend/data/
/data/
.claudio/
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.log
**/*.pid

# --- Local config & secrets --------------------------------------------------
claudio-backend/config/config.yaml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Host-only scratch / non-deployed content --------------------------------
*.bat
temp/
todo/
doc/
